Rejected after full-paper review. The native family passes G and V but fails H on both tracks.

Section 3, Case 2 directly produces the compressed Hamiltonian word using two subtractions. Increasing \(p,q,r,s\) enlarges only its repetition count; it does not increase certificate-production difficulty. Full-cycle expansion is expensive, but that is output/verification work, not a distinct Track B mechanical search.

Details and measurements are in [REJECTED.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2107.14787/REJECTED.md). The audited prototype is retained as [rejected_gen_2107_14787.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2107.14787/rejected_gen_2107_14787.py), as required.

Source: [arXiv:2107.14787](https://arxiv.org/abs/2107.14787).
